---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import TokenTable from "../components/api/TokenTable.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "behavior", label: "Behavior" },
  { id: "validation", label: "Type validation" },
  { id: "tokens", label: "Tokens" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="drop_zone" sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          A <code>.drop-zone</code> is a large target for choosing files. Put
          an icon, a prompt and a native <code>&lt;input type="file"&gt;</code>
          inside a <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. Add an optional
          <code>.drop-zone-files</code> list to show what was chosen.
        </p>
        <p>
          The CSS stretches the input invisibly over the whole label. A click,
          Enter, Space or a dropped file reaches it exactly as it would a
          plain file input, and the label text names it. For a compact
          button and path field, use the
          <a href={route('text_inputs') + '#file'}>file input</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="drop-zone" style="max-width: 32rem;">
          <label>
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">upload_file</span>
            Drop files here or browse
            <small>PDF or PNG files</small>
            <input type="file" multiple accept=".pdf,.png">
          </label>
          <ul class="drop-zone-files" aria-live="polite"></ul>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="drop-zone">
  <label>
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">upload_file</span>
    Drop files here or browse
    <small>PDF or PNG files</small>
    <input type="file" multiple accept=".pdf,.png">
  </label>
  <ul class="drop-zone-files" aria-live="polite"></ul>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.behavior}>
        <p>
          Add <code>multiple</code> to the input to take several files at
          once. A dropped file replaces the selection, as it does on any file
          input. The Forms behavior adds <code>dragover</code> to the zone
          while files are over it. It fills <code>.drop-zone-files</code> with
          each file's name and size, formatted for the page's locale. It
          listens on the document, so zones added later work too. Resetting
          the form empties the list after reset dispatch finishes; a canceled
          reset preserves it. A newer selection keeps its list and feedback.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>accept</code> is a picker hint. Opt into the type validation
          below for matching checks on both browse and drop selections.
          Check received files on the server; metadata does not verify contents.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.validation}>
    <p>
      Add <code>data-validate-types</code> to the native input to check every
      selected file against <code>accept</code>. One unsupported file
      invalidates the whole selection and blocks normal native form submission.
      Every selected file stays in the input and optional list. Unmarked zones
      keep their existing picker-hint behavior.
    </p>
    <div class="drop-zone" style="max-width:32rem;">
      <label>Drop documents here or browse
        <small>PDF or PNG files</small>
        <input type="file" multiple data-validate-types accept=".pdf,.png">
      </label>
      <p class="supporting-text" data-error="Choose PDF or PNG files." role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
      <ul class="drop-zone-files" aria-live="polite"></ul>
    </div>
    <Code code={`
<div class="drop-zone">
  <label>Drop documents here or browse
    <small>PDF or PNG files</small>
    <input type="file" multiple data-validate-types accept=".pdf,.png">
  </label>
  <p class="supporting-text" data-error="Choose PDF or PNG files."
     role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
  <ul class="drop-zone-files" aria-live="polite"></ul>
</div>
`} />
    <p>
      Match extensions such as <code>.pdf</code> or <code>.tar.gz</code>, exact
      MIME types without parameters, such as <code>application/pdf</code>, or <code>image/*</code>,
      <code>audio/*</code> and <code>video/*</code>. Comma-separated alternatives
      are trimmed and case-insensitive. Empty MIME types can match an explicit
      extension, but do not match MIME-only rules. Unsupported tokens are ignored;
      missing, empty or wholly unsupported accept values impose no type restriction.
    </p>
    <p>
      Supply the direct <code>[data-error]</code> status area even without a
      file list. Its data-error value customizes the type message; an empty
      value uses a message naming accept. The runtime writes real text,
      appends its id once to the input's <code>aria-describedby</code>, and
      updates <code>aria-invalid</code> without moving focus. Required fields
      and application custom errors remain effective. Existing application
      custom validity takes precedence over the native type message; the status
      can still explain a type mismatch.
    </p>
    <p>
      Valid replacement, clearing or an uncanceled reset releases only the
      framework's type error. Remaining native/application errors stay visible.
      Canceled resets preserve the current view. Disabled controls remain
      inactive; after enabling or changing files/constraints from script, call
      <code>Expressive.Forms.validateField(input)</code> to refresh validity and
      feedback silently. A bubbling composed input or change also refreshes
      the file list. Both paths work in open shadow roots.
    </p>
    <p>
      A changed invalid selection reports one bubbling, composed, noncancelable
      <code>expressive:reject</code> from the zone with
      <code>{"{ input, files, rejected, reason: 'type' }"}</code>.
      File arrays are snapshots. A native input/change pair reports once;
      silent validation and reset report no rejection. This is a notification,
      so canceling it cannot allow invalid files. Size/count limits and uploads
      are outside this option. Native novalidate/formnovalidate bypasses remain
      native; always validate received files on the server.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.tokens}>
        <p>Override these on the <code>.drop-zone</code>.</p>
        <TokenTable>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-drop-zone-shape</code></td>
            <td>16px</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-drop-zone-outline-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-outline</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-drop-zone-dragover-container-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-primary-container</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-drop-zone-dragover-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-on-primary-container</code></td>
          </tr>
        </TokenTable>
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
